# Yoink 🎬

> **The ultimate self-hosted YouTube downloader ecosystem.**  
> Powered by a lightweight **Chrome Extension (MV3)** and a high-performance **Node.js + `yt-dlp` backend**.

![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)
![Manifest](https://img.shields.io/badge/chrome%20extension-MV3-green.svg)
![Backend](https://img.shields.io/badge/backend-Node.js%20%7C%20yt--dlp-red.svg)

---

## ✨ Features

- ⚡ **Native YouTube Integration:** Automatically injects clean "Download" buttons beneath YouTube videos, Shorts, and playlist pages.
- 🎬 **4K & 8K Video Quality:** Select resolution (144p to 4320p/8K), frame rates (60fps), and codecs (H.264, VP9, AV1).
- 🎵 **High-Bitrate Audio:** One-click extraction to 320kbps MP3, M4A, WAV, or FLAC with automatically embedded album art and metadata.
- 🚫 **SponsorBlock Integration:** Strip out sponsored segments, self-promotions, intros, and outros on download.
- 📝 **Subtitles & Captions:** Download auto-generated or manual subtitles in `.srt` or `.vtt` formats, or embed them directly into video containers.
- 📚 **Full Playlist Support:** Select individual videos or download entire playlists with organized folder hierarchies.
- 📊 **Real-Time Websocket Updates:** Live progress tracking, speed gauges, and ETA readouts powered by Socket.IO.
- 🔒 **100% Private:** Processing happens locally on your own machine. Zero third-party telemetry, tracking, or account requirements.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

```text
YOUTUBE WEBPAGE
                         │
                         ▼
             ┌──────────────────────┐
             │ Content Script       │  (Injects native download UI)
             │ (content.js)         │
             └───────────┬──────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
             ┌──────────────────────┐
             │ Service Worker       │  (Context menus & notifications)
             │ (background.js)      │
             └───────────┬──────────┘
                         │
        ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
        ▼                                 ▼
┌──────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────┐
│ Extension Popup UI   │          │ Full Dashboard UI    │
│ (popup.html)         │          │ (dashboard.html)     │
└───────────┬──────────┘          └───────────┬──────────┘
│                                 │
└────────────────┬────────────────┘
│ REST / WebSockets (localhost:4000)
▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ Node.js Backend      │  (Express, Socket.IO)
│ (server.js)          │
└───────────┬──────────┘
│
▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│    yt-dlp + FFmpeg   │  (Core download engine)
└──────────────────────┘
```

---

## 📋 Prerequisites

Before running Yoink, ensure you have the following installed on your host system:

1. **[Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)** (v18.0.0 or higher)
2. **[yt-dlp](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp)** (Must be added to system PATH)
3. **[FFmpeg](https://ffmpeg.org)** (Required for audio extraction, merging formats, and subtitle embedding)

---

## 🚀 Quick Start Guide

### 1. Set Up the Backend Server
```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/yoink.git
cd yoink/backend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start the local server
node server.js
```
The backend server will run on `http://localhost:4000`.

### 2. Load the Chrome Extension
1. Open Google Chrome and navigate to `chrome://extensions/`.
2. Enable **Developer mode** using the toggle switch in the top right corner.
3. Click **Load unpacked**.
4. Select the extension folder you downloaded using the git command.

Navigate to any YouTube video—you will see the ⬇ **Download** button integrated directly into the page!
